  {
    "taxonId": 210414,
    "summary": "Herbaceous flowering plant native to the Mediterranean region. It has bright blue flowers and blackish roots that are blue-red inside; the roots yield a red dye used since antiquity and to colour some cheeses and wines.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "Root dye colours some cheeses and low-quality wines; alkannin is approved as food colouring in Australia, but EU approval has been withdrawn.",
    "evidence": {
